        "en": "The people of Lut were the best of the people God created, but Iblis pursued them intensely. When they went out to work, they all went together, leaving the women behind. Iblis would visit their belongings, and when they returned, he would ruin what they had done. Some said to others, 'Let us ambush the one who ruins our belongings.' They ambushed him and found him to be a beautiful boy. They asked, 'Are you the one who ruins our belongings?' He said, 'Yes, time and again.' They agreed to kill him and set an ambush at a man's house. At night, the boy cried out. The man asked, 'What is wrong with you?' He said, 'My father used to put me to sleep on my stomach.' The man said, 'Come, sleep on my stomach.' The boy kept rubbing him until he taught him to perform the act with himself. First, Iblis did it, then the boy did it. Then he slipped away and fled from them. In the morning, the man informed them of what the boy had done, and they were pleased with something they did not know. They placed their hands on him until the men were satisfied with one another. Then they began to ambush whoever passed by the road and did to them what they did, until the people left their city. Then they left their women and turned to the boys. When Iblis saw that he had perfected his matter with the men, he turned to the women and made himself a woman. He said, 'Your men do to one another.' They said, 'Yes, we have seen that.' And Lut used to admonish and advise them, until he was slighted by them. Then the women conspired with the women. When the argument was complete against them, God sent Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil in the guise of boys, wearing caps. They passed by Lut (peace be upon him) while he was plowing. He said, 'Where are you going? I have never seen anyone more beautiful than you.' They said, 'Our master sent us to the Lord of this city.' He said, 'Has your master not reached what the people of this village do? O my sons, by God, they take men and do to them until blood comes out.' They said, 'Our master commanded us to pass through the middle of it.' He said, 'I have a need for you.' They said, 'What is it?' He said, 'You stay here until the mixing of darkness.' He said, so they sat. He sent his daughter and said, 'Bring them bread, bring them water in a skin, and bring them a cloak to cover themselves from the cold.' When the daughter went to the house, the rain came from the valley. He said to them, 'Rise, let us go.' Lut (peace be upon him) walked at the base of the wall, while Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil walked in the middle of the road. He said, 'O my sons, walk here.' They said, 'Our master commanded us to pass through the middle of it.' Lut (peace be upon him) was waiting for the darkness. Iblis passed by and took a child from the lap of a woman and threw him into the well. All the people of the city cried out at the door of Lut (peace be upon him). When they looked at the boys in Lut's house, they said, 'O Lut, you have entered into our work.' He said, 'These are my guests, so do not disgrace me.' They said, 'Take one and give us two.' He said, and he brought them into the chamber. Lut (peace be upon him) said, 'If I had a family to protect me from you.' They pushed against the door, broke the door of Lut (peace be upon him), and threw Lut down. Gabriel said to them, 'We are the messengers of your Lord; they will not reach you. Take a handful of dust from the earth and strike their faces.' He said, 'The faces were struck, and all the people of the city went blind. Lut (peace be upon him) said to them, 'O messengers of my Lord, what did your Lord command you regarding them?' They said, 'He commanded us to take them at dawn.' He said, 'I have a need for you.' They said, 'What is your need?' He said, 'Take them immediately.' They said, 'O Lut, their appointment is morning. Is morning not near to you? But we want you to depart. Take your daughters and go, and leave your wife.' Abu Ja'far (peace be upon him) said, 